it fan produced? Were there any other City of the Damned books written?</div> </div> </div> </div>MrGone's <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/fanbooks.html\" target=\"_blank\">website</a> lists it as a fanbook.<br /> <br /> The only official &quot;City of the Damned&quot; book for Requiem is City of the Damned: New Orleans, in the same vein as Hunting Ground: the Rockies was a setting book for Werewolf: the Forsaken, Boston Unveiled was a setting book for Mage: the Awakening, and Splintered City: Seattle (albeit much later) was a setting book for Demon: the Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T16:40:43-07:00","id":1506802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cabaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506793-city-of-the-damned-los-angeles#post1506793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some time ago, I read an interesting book for Vampire the Requiem. It was City of the Damned - Los Angeles. Nice reading, in what context was it written? Was it fan produced? Were there any other City of the Damned books written?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like a book for Demon the Fallen, than VtR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 03-28-2023, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T16:55:03-07:00","id":1506804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506793-city-of-the-damned-los-angeles?p=1506795#post1506795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MrGone's <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/fanbooks.html\" target=\"_blank\">website</a> lists it as a fanbook.<br /> <br /> The only official &quot;City of the Damned&quot; book for Requiem is City of the Damned: New Orleans, in the same vein as Hunting Ground: the Rockies was a setting book for Werewolf: the Forsaken, Boston Unveiled was a setting book for Mage: the Awakening, and Splintered City: Seattle (albeit much later) was a setting book for Demon: the Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, from there they pretty much jumped to regional/country scale with Shadows of Mexico (mainly Requiem but with some stuff on other lines) &amp; UK (idem, but for Forsaken) and then pretty much left the idea of such books aside, writing ones in how to breath (unnatural) life into one's fictional version of a real or created city instead (Damnation City, Block by Bloody Block), if memory tricks me not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T15:59:12-07:00","id":1507127,"title":"","content":"I do, have an age-old project I've been working on called, &quot;The City of Angels&quot;, which, started out as a fictional-WoD city and goes from there. It will have seven-hills reflecting, you know. I've yet to fully commit to an era, either film-noir or modern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T06:25:46-07:00","id":1512281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <stron